262
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,480
 Isn't that interesting?

263
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:04,520
 They simultaneously forget his goodness

264
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,320
 'cause they worship something else.

265
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:09,080
 So all the people, they took off the rings of gold

266
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,400
 that were in their ears and they brought them to Aaron

267
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,880
 and he received the gold from their hand

268
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,640
 and he fashioned it with a graving tool

269
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,080
 and he made a golden calf and they said,

270
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:17,120
 "These are your gods of Israel

271
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,600
 "who brought you up out of the land of Egypt."

272
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,440
 We'll stop there.

273
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:23,800
 Now at first glance, there's a good chance

274
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:26,080
 you're reading this and you're like,

275
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:28,320
 "What the heck is even going on?"

276
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,800
 Not because this is confusing

277
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,240
 and it's difficult to understand,

278
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:32,920
 it's difficult to relate to.

279
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,600
 Like I don't imagine anybody in here

280
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,640
 is like cooking up an idol in the back.

281
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,760
 No one's got a block of wood

282
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,720
 that they're kind of shaping up

283
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,040
 because they're gonna set it in an altar

284
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,280
 and they're gonna worship when they get home.

285
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,400
 Most people are not indulging

286
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:46,000
 this specific practice here today.

287
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,080
 And so we read this and we're like,

288
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:50,080
 "Goodness gracious, like how antiquated are they?

289
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,640
 "What are they even thinking about doing?"

290
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:54,680
 And yet the truth of the matter is we do this ourselves.

291
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,760
 You see, we could actually hop in a time machine

292
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,280
 and take ourselves back to the ancient Near East.

293
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:01,280
 What we would realize is they have very good reason

294
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:04,000
 for actually indulging idolatry.

295
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,440
 They have three reasons specifically.

296
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:08,880
 They have the reasons of control, acceptance, and permission.

297
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,680
 That's why people made idols for themselves.

298
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:14,200
 They would make idols for the simple sake of control.

299
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:17,680
 Because the idea was is that the moment an idol was carved,

300
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,760
 the God that that idol represented

301
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:23,280
 would embody the statue itself.

302
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:26,400
 And that meant that God was present with you immediately.

303
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,480
 And so now you have the ability with him right there,

304
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,320
 or her right there to manage and manipulate

305
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:34,080
 and get out of that God whatever it is that you wanted.

306
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:37,000
 How many of you are so annoyed

307
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,840
 with the reality that you have to trust in God?

308
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,840
 With an idol, you don't.

309
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,400
 With an idol, you don't have to trust God

310
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,440
 because you can control God.

311
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,800
 See the appeal?

312
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,200
 That's why they did it.

313
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,560
 And now listen, we don't do this.

314
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:50,720
 I'm not necessarily expecting

315
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,760
 that any of you are carving calves at home,

316
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:55,360
 but we still try to control our outcomes nonetheless,

317
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,520
 don't we?

318
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,600
 You build five-year plans, you obsess over your

319
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,320
 career trajectories, you move cities

320
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,720
 because there's a better dating opportunity,

321
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:05,720
 all because you wanna make sure your life turns out

322
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,320
 the way you want your life to turn out.

323
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,600
 It looks different in 2026,

324
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,120
 but the impulse is the same nonetheless.

325
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,880
 We want control.

326
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,920
 The second reason that they would carve idols

327
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,720
 is because an idol would offer them acceptance.

328
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,920
 It would offer them acceptance.

329
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,600
 The nations surrounding Israel at this time,

330
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:24,040
 they all worshiped idols.

331
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,680
 Everybody worshiped idols.

332
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:28,960
 And so to fit in, you did so similarly.

333
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,880
 Like there were gods for everything in this time,

334
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:34,000
 gods for pregnancy and harvest and conquest and vitality.

335
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,640
 And so the beauty of this was for that time,

336
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:40,280
 it was not just acceptable, it was expected.

337
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:42,520
 Like everybody does it, so you should do it too.

338
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,560
 Again, I don't think that anybody here

339
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,800
 is necessarily thinking to themselves,

340
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,120
 like I must bow to Baal.

341
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,280
 And yet the truth of the matter is,

342
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,800
 you walked into this room and you nonetheless

343
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,200
 asked a similar question, how do I fit in here?

344
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,360
 And because you're desperate to fit in,

345
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:59,080
 you obsess over how you look and what you drive

346
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:01,200
 and what you make and where you're going

347
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,480
 and who your friends are, all of the details

348
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,960
 about your life you are so fixated on

349
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:09,080
 because you want acceptance.

350
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,920
 And the third reason they would worship idols

351
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,160
 is because it gave them permission.

352
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,560
 Permission.

353
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,240
 You see, idolatry gave you the permission

354
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,920
 to live your life however you wanted.

355
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:22,720
 And specifically for them, it gave them permission

356
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:27,200
 to indulge their promiscuity, their sexual desire.

357
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:32,560
 We don't necessarily do the same

358
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:35,760
 in the sense that we don't believe sex on earth

359
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:37,360
 means sex in heaven, and so sex in heaven

360
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,640
 produces big rain and big crops and big livestock.

361
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:42,960
 None of you are checking the yield on your crops this year.

362
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,600
 And yet the truth of the matter is,

363
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:52,280
 the world, and Christians included, nonetheless,

364
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:54,440
 don't permission to sleep with whoever they want

365
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,400
 whenever they want.

366
00:13:55,400 --> 00:14:00,880
 You see, idolatry, it takes a relationship

367
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:03,800
 that was designed to be God-centered,

368
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,520
 and it makes it me-centered.

369
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:11,160
 It inverts the entire relational paradigm.

370
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:14,360
 You see, no longer do I exist for God.

371
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,440
 God exists for me.

372
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,040
 How does that happen?

373
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,760
 How do we get in a situation where everything

374
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,040
 was upside down from what God actually intended?

375
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,920
 Well, that's what I want to tell you.

376
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:27,120
 The way that idolatry happens, first and foremost,

377
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:30,760
 is idolatry begins with getting used to God.

378
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,680
 Idolatry begins by getting used to God.

379
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:33,560
 Look at verse one.

380
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,800
 It says, "The people saw that Moses delayed

381
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:38,040
 "to come down from the mountain."

382
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,200
 They saw that Moses delayed.

383
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:43,400
 This is crazy, because what's happening in the moment?

384
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:48,400
 That the presence of God has descended on Mount Sinai,

385
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:52,000
 like thunder and fire and wind and smoke

386
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:56,800
 and all of the honor and glory of God is upon that mountain.

387
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,640
 He has come to covenant with his people,

388
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,960
 have everlasting relationship with them.

389
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,040
 This is what's happening in the moment,

390
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,880
 and yet they don't realize that.

391
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:09,120
 They just realize that our guy Mo hasn't come down yet.

392
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:11,400
 How does that happen?

393
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:17,480
 Because they got used to God's presence.

394
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,600
 They got used to his presence.

395
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,240
 And the same thing happens to us.

396
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,120
 We find ourselves getting used to God's presence

397
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:25,000
 and his provision and his power,

398
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,840
 and the reason why is because we've been at this

399
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,280
 for a long time.

400
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:32,280
 The crazy thing for them is they were there for 40 days,

401
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,920
 and just 40 days later, they're already tired of it, man.

402
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,200
 They're bored with the whole thing

403
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,960
 that they've been called into,

404
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,000
 and so they start looking to the left and to the right

405
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,440
 for something else to appeal to their interests.

406
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:44,280
 Do we not do the same?

407
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:45,120
 Why?

408
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,400
 Why does it happen?

409
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,800
 Well, I'll share a story that I think might help.

410
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:52,200
 My sister, years ago, it's not what she does anymore,

411
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,960
 but years ago, she nannied for one of the wealthiest families

412
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,160
 in the city of Dallas.

413
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,440
 I don't know how she landed in the gig,

414
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:02,080
 but she found a job, and what she had to do one summer

415
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:05,000
 is she had to watch the kids in this family

416
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,640
 as the family took a three-month-long cruise

417
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:10,200
 across the Caribbean in their private yacht.

418
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,000
 It was a really tough job, but someone's gotta do it.

419
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,640
 And so she decided that she was gonna make the most

420
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,480
 of the experience.

421
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,640
 She gets out there, and while she's doing it,

422
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,840
 she's experiencing the most amazing places,

423
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:22,520
 like they're at St. Lucia, and Anguilla, and Aruba,

424
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:25,080
 and the Bahamas, and the Grand Cayman Islands.

425
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:26,960
 They're doing all of the amazing things,

426
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,800
 meeting the most amazing people,

427
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:29,280
 eating the most amazing food, seeing the most amazing sights.

428
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:32,000
 They are having the best time of their lives,

429
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,800
 and yet when she comes back, and we're catching up,

430
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,440
 and I'm like, "Tell me all about it,"

431
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:36,680
 she's like, "You wanna know what the spiritual crisis

432
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:37,640
 "of my summer was?

433
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:41,240
 "I would've killed for a hamburger and French fries."

434
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,680
 And I was like, "That's it?

435
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,160
 "That's what you wanted?

436
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:48,120
 "You were experiencing the most amazing thing,

437
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:50,800
 "and yet all you wanted was a Big Mac?

438
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:52,680
 "Like, come on, man, that feels wild."

439
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:55,000
 And yet the reality of it was this.

440
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,480
 It's not that the Caribbean became less beautiful.

441
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:01,640
 It's that she became accustomed to beautiful things.

442
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:04,680
 That's what happens to you.

443
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:05,880
 It's what happens to me.

444
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:09,600
 We get used to being in the presence of God.

445
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:13,080
 We get used to his power in our lives.

446
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:18,400
 That's why we wake up and we drag ourselves to quiet time,

447
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:22,560
 because it's a non-negotiable, I'm supposed to do this,

448
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:25,920
 it's a rite of passage, it's a civil duty I must do

449
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,520
 according to the kingdom of God.

450
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,720
 It's why your prayers feel so forced.

451
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,440
 It's why your worship feels so tired.

452
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:35,480
 It's why coming to church feels coerced.

453
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:40,440
 It's like why all of the regular rites of our Christianity

454
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:43,160
 feel so very difficult to indulge

455
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:46,040
 because they've just become so normal.

456
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:48,040
 They've just become so bored.

457
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:51,320
 And so what ends up happening

458
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:54,000
 is we stop focusing on all that we have in God

459
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,360
 and we start focusing on all that we do not have instead,

460
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,400
 which is the second reason idolatry happens.

461
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:03,800
 Idolatry grows when we're discontent with God.

462
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:08,080
 It begins because you're used to him, you're bored with him,

463
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:11,880
 but it grows when we are discontent with him.

464
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,200
 Like we stop focusing on what he's given

465
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,360
 and we start focusing on everything that he hasn't,

466
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,440
 that God hasn't given me that relationship yet,

467
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,160
 that God hasn't given me that job yet,

468
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,440
 that God hasn't given me clarity about my future yet,

469
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:23,400
 that God hasn't given me the life that I dreamt

470
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,720
 that he was going to give me, he hasn't given me that yet.

471
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:28,040
 And as we realize all the things

472
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,680
 that God has yet to give us,

473
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:33,400
 and we fail to remember everything he's already afforded us,

474
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:36,160
 what we decide is that if God won't give me what I want,

475
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,960
 then I'll find something that will.

476
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,320
 That's where golden calf comes from.

477
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:45,720
 That's where idolatry springs up.

478
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:49,600
 Because it leads us to do pretty crazy things

479
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:51,000
 when we're in this spot.

480
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,080
 I've seen it, like I've seen guys take jobs

481
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:57,240
 they have no interest in solely because it pays well.

482
00:18:57,240 --> 00:19:01,720
 I've seen girls date absolute losers

483
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,720
 because they just want to find love.

484
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:08,240
 I've seen friends compromise their moral integrity

485
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,720
 because they just want to fit in.

486
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:13,520
 I've seen believers lie, bold-faced lie to others

487
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:16,000
 because they want to preserve their reputation.

488
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,240
 This happens all over the grade.

489
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,080
 When I was in college ministry,

490
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:21,160
 I remember seeing this what it felt like on a weekly basis.

491
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,600
 There was like a young lady in our ministry

492
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:27,320
 who she showed up and she was in a position

493
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:31,560
 where she desperately wanted to get this job.

494
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:33,440
 And the opportunity came for her to get that job.

495
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,760
 And she didn't necessarily want to take the job

496
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,640
 because she was interested in the job.

497
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,560
 She just wanted the job because the job really paid well.

498
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:42,320
 And it felt like that was a repeat soundtrack in my life.

499
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:45,880
 I remember years later visiting with a friend

500
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:48,320
 who actually, he did the same thing.

501
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:52,800
 His experience was one where he landed the gig,

502
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:56,320
 like the job that everybody would have killed for.

503
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,920
 He was one of two people hired for.

504
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:01,680
 And this job, it was prolific for two things in specific.

505
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,960
 It was prolific for the fact that

506
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:07,080
 they paid ridiculous amounts of money.

507
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:10,000
 And it was also prolific because they worked their employees

508
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,840
 ridiculous kinds of hours.

509
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:14,600
 And as we sat there a couple of years later

510
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:15,720
 from the time that he took the job,

511
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:18,800
 he walked in, he looked like a shell of himself.

512
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:25,160
 And as we sat down and he pulled out not one,

513
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:31,160
 not two, but three phones, all of which were work-related.

514
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:35,480
 I remember asking him, how's the job?

515
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:39,720
 And he said, I'm a miserable man.

516
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:43,400
 I hate my job.

517
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:46,480
 I get no sleep and I have no life.

518
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:52,080
 But where else can I go to make this kind of money, right?

519
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:55,320
 And I remember thinking to myself,

520
00:20:55,320 --> 00:21:05,000
 you're choosing the job instead of God.

521
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:08,680
 You're choosing this to provide for you

522
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,160
 instead of him to provide for you.

523
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:13,080
 And as sad as that seems to us,

524
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,920
 like even just the emotional reactions in the room,

525
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,720
 we do this, this is us.

526
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:21,120
 We're a part of this same kind of decision-making.

527
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:24,920
 Like we can't help ourselves from doing likewise.

528
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,480
 Like the Israelites, they do it themselves.

529
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,000
 They literally, it says right here,

530
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,120
 hey, make us gods that shall go before us.

531
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,200
 Why do they say that?

532
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:33,480
 Why do they look at Aaron and they're like,

533
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,840
 hey, make us gods who will go before us.

534
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:36,200
 The language there is interesting.

535
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,200
 Make us gods who will go before us.

536
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:41,200
 What God went before them in getting into this moment.

537
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:44,320
 Yahweh, like the God of Israel.

538
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,800
 He's the one that led them here.

539
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,000
 And yet that God,

540
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,160
 he's still swirling up on the mountain, I guess.

541
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,920
 Our boy Moses, he's trapped up there.

542
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:51,760
 We have no idea.

543
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:52,600
 Nobody's heard from him.

544
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,040
 Guess he lost cell reception.

545
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:55,080
 And so I guess, you know what?

546
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:57,080
 We need a new God who will take us out of here

547
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,960
 to the very place that we want to go.

548
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,880
 We want to go to the promised land.

549
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,560
 And so yeah, we could go on God's time,

550
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,080
 but we'd much rather go on our time.

551
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:06,360
 We'll wait instead

552
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:12,440
 for our desire instead of God's.

553
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:15,720
 We'll get up and we'll move ourselves out

554
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:17,600
 as opposed to wait for him to do so.

555
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:19,800
 And the truth of the matter is,

556
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:21,720
 like they wanted so badly for the promised land.

557
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,040
 They wanted to get there as quickly as they could.

558
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:26,040
 And I can't help but wonder how many of us in this room

559
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:28,640
 are in a similar place that are just dying

560
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:32,920
 to get into whatever your proverbial promised land is.

561
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:35,520
 To get into that job, that relationship, that body,

562
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:37,920
 that tax bracket, that group of friends,

563
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:41,160
 that level of influence that you'll bail on God

564
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,200
 the way they bailed on God

565
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,400
 just so you can get there as soon as you can.

566
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:48,200
 I've been there.

567
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,040
 I've done that.

568
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:53,120
 And it never works well.

569
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:58,600
 It never works well when we want the promised land

570
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,040
 more than the promised maker,

571
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,680
 which is exactly what they did.

572
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:04,440
 Now, let me be very clear.

573
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:08,000
 Some of you are like, but my promised land doesn't feel bad.

574
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,200
 Theirs wasn't.

575
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,040
 Their promised land was great.

576
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,160
 Land flowing with milk and honey.

577
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:13,080
 Anybody want to move in?

578
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,160
 I'm like, that sounds awesome.

579
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:17,640
 I don't even know what that means, but it sounds great.

580
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:22,080
 I'd take that over 105 degree heat in Texas summer.

581
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:25,720
 And yet the truth is, as great as it is,

582
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,960
 as good as the promised land is,

583
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,840
 a good thing can become a dangerous thing

584
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:32,560
 whenever it becomes an ultimate thing.

585
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:34,880
 And so many of us, we have good things in our lives

586
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:37,840
 that we desperately want, that have become ultimate things

587
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,320
 that we've placed above God,

588
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,280
 that we want more than we want Him.

589
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:43,320
 Tim Keller says it this way.

590
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:45,920
 He says, "When anything in life is an absolute requirement

591
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:48,440
 "for your happiness and self-worth,

592
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:50,520
 "it's essentially an idol,

593
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:52,320
 "something that you're worshiping."

594
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:54,800
 And that's the scariest part.

595
00:23:54,800 --> 00:24:01,240
 But the minute you want something more than God,

596
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,400
 it's not that you stop worshiping Him.

597
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:08,200
 It's just that you start worshiping something else,

598
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:11,840
 which is what happens in the story.

599
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:13,880
 It says in verse five, "When Aaron saw this,"

600
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:14,760
 talking about the golden calf,

601
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:16,600
 "he built an altar before it,

602
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:19,760
 "and he made a proclamation that said,

603
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:21,440
 "'Tomorrow shall be a feast to the Lord.'

604
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:23,080
 "And so they rose up early the next day,

605
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,280
 "and they offered burnt offerings,

606
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,400
 "and they brought peace offerings.

607
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,960
 "And the people sat down to eat and drink,

608
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:30,080
 "and they rose up to play."

609
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:32,160
 In some scriptures, different translations,

610
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:33,760
 "Rose up to play" is the word revelry.

611
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:37,960
 It has the connotation of sexual promiscuity.

612
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:39,760
 They just started to sleep together.

613
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:43,320
 And the reason why all of this happens

614
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:46,520
 is because though idolatry begins

615
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:49,120
 with getting used to God,

616
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:52,840
 and it grows from a discontentment with God,

617
00:24:52,840 --> 00:24:56,440
 is it ultimately redefines the worship of God.

618
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:58,040
 It redefines the worship of God.

619
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:00,680
 Because here's the thing

620
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:01,880
 that you need to notice about the story,

621
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:03,640
 and it's subtle, but it's true.

622
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:06,400
 The golden calf was not a replacement for God.

623
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:10,960
 It was a redefinition of God.

624
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:13,720
 And you just read it, and you can see the examples.

625
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:16,320
 Like Aaron builds an altar to it.

626
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:19,120
 Where do you think he learned the idea of building altars?

627
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:22,000
 That was an instruction given from Yahweh,

628
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,280
 from the God of Israel himself.

629
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:28,200
 He proclaims a feast to the all-caps LORD,

630
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,520
 meaning the covenantal name of Yahweh,

631
00:25:30,520 --> 00:25:34,440
 like the feast that they're giving is to Yahweh.

632
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:36,000
 And they're still bringing burnt offerings

633
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,280
 and peace offerings, why?

634
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,280
 Because they still love God.

635
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:41,000
 They just wanna do whatever the heck they wanna do.

636
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:41,960
 They wanna eat, and they wanna drink,

637
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:44,600
 and they wanna have sex with whoever they wish.

638
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,960
 It would be the equivalent of this.

639
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:48,280
 It would be the equivalent of someone saying,

640
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:50,360
 "Hey, I really wanna lose weight,

641
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:52,280
 "and I wanna eat an entire pizza."

642
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:54,920
 And you'd be like, "That doesn't work.

643
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,560
 "Like that is impossible.

644
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:57,600
 "It doesn't make any sense.

645
00:25:57,600 --> 00:26:00,560
 "Like that won't allow you to get where you're trying to go."

646
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:02,840
 Or if someone came to you, and instead,

647
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:03,680
 they were like, "Man, hey,

648
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,040
 "I really wanna take some time off work,

649
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:06,840
 "but I don't wanna take any vacation time."

650
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:08,320
 You'd be like, "You're fired, you know?

651
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:09,400
 "Like that's not how this works.

652
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,720
 "You're not allowed to do that.

653
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:11,800
 "It doesn't make sense.

654
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:16,800
 "You cannot want two opposing ideas

655
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:19,200
 "that will achieve the same inevitable end.

656
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:20,080
 "That doesn't work.

657
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:21,920
 "What's the phrase of speech?

658
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:24,080
 "You can't have your cake and eat it too."

659
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:25,720
 That's what they're trying to do.

660
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:29,360
 And we do this as well.

661
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:34,280
 I used to see it in college ministry all the time.

662
00:26:34,280 --> 00:26:37,560
 I would see it with a young lady that was in our ministry.

663
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:38,560
 Like she would come to us,

664
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:42,000
 and she had a really hard past, a really difficult story,

665
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:44,640
 and yet she found herself like loving the people of God,

666
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:48,560
 and so invested in her community and Christian friends,

667
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:53,560
 and yet she nonetheless actively lived a gay lifestyle.

668
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:57,920
 We had another young man in the same ministry

669
00:26:57,920 --> 00:27:00,960
 who he was so bought in

670
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:03,800
 on everything that was happening in the ministry.

671
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:06,840
 He had great buddies that were all holding him accountable,

672
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:10,000
 and yet he was nonetheless sleeping with his girlfriend.

673
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,240
 And I remember looking at both of them

674
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,640
 and just like leaning in very gently

675
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:15,160
 and pressing on the issue and just asking like,

676
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:17,080
 "Hey, how does this work?"

677
00:27:17,080 --> 00:27:18,760
 Because there's an incompatibility here.

678
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:21,200
 Like you can't claim to love Christ

679
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:24,800
 and likewise live for the things that he died

680
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:26,200
 to free you from.

681
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,480
 How does that happen?

682
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,680
 There's an incompatibility.

683
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:30,880
 And I remember the answers they would give

684
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:32,520
 were things like,

685
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:35,360
 "But come on, man, like there's grace for that, right?

686
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:36,760
 "God just wants me to be happy.

687
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:38,040
 "Like it's not that big of a deal.

688
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:42,120
 "Like surely God isn't, he's not to eat up over this."

689
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:43,840
 And what I learned in that moment

690
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:47,320
 is like they didn't want to replace God.

691
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:52,120
 They just wanted to redefine him to fit their own desires.

692
00:27:52,120 --> 00:27:54,560
 And we do this.

693
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:56,000
 Here's the thing.

694
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:56,840
 We do it, man.

695
00:27:56,840 --> 00:28:00,280
 Like we were praying in here earlier,

696
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:02,280
 me and my team, and there was just this,

697
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:10,240
 this suspicion that when the topic of idolatry comes up,

698
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:11,720
 we would think it's someone else's problem

699
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:14,320
 when the reality is it's everyone's problem.

700
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:19,640
 Like idolatry is the beginning of all sin.

701
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:22,960
 It's the worship of something other than God,

702
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:27,360
 which means every single person in this room is an idolater.

703
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:30,000
 And the reason why all of us are subject to it

704
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:33,520
 is because we are redefining God to meet our own desire.

705
00:28:33,520 --> 00:28:35,480
 Like some of you, you're redefining him

706
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:38,000
 so you can watch porn whenever you want it.

707
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:40,080
 Some of you, you're redefining God

708
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:42,720
 so you can drink just to unwind at the end of the day,

709
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,760
 even if it leads you to the point

710
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:44,840
 of having a little bit too much.

711
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:46,000
 Some of you, you're redefining him

712
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,720
 so you can gossip behind that person's back.

713
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:48,800
 Others of you, you're redefining him

714
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:51,120
 so you can justify what you post online.

715
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:53,400
 I could go on, but here's the truth of the matter.

716
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:56,040
 Idolatry is not just saying, "I don't want God."

717
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:58,240
 What it is saying is, "I want God.

718
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:00,200
 "I just want him on my own terms."

719
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:04,520
 And so many of us are guilty of it.

720
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:08,760
 But what happens in that world

721
00:29:08,760 --> 00:29:10,520
 is we end up with a version of God

722
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:15,280
 that is not consistent with the one true God.

723
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:20,840
 James 4:4 says, "You adulterous people,

724
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:24,280
 "do you not know that friendship with the world

725
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:25,320
 "is enmity with God?

726
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:27,560
 "You cannot have them both.

727
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:30,080
 "Therefore, whoever wishes to be a friend of the world

728
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:31,720
 "makes himself an enemy of God."

729
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:36,320
 You see, when you have an incomplete view of God,

730
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:38,520
 you will have an incorrect response to God.

731
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:41,680
 And it's very dangerous ground

732
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:44,680
 when we start bending our theology to accommodate our lusts.

733
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:48,840
 When we take the portions of God that we like

734
00:29:48,840 --> 00:29:51,600
 and we discard the portions that we don't.

735
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:54,000
 How do you think that would work in my marriage?

736
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:57,600
 If I only interacted with Brooke

737
00:29:57,600 --> 00:30:01,320
 on the basis of the qualities that I liked about her,

738
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:02,960
 I think it would go really bad.

739
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:06,160
 I love that she's gracious,

740
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,600
 so I guess I'll just use that to flirt

741
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:09,120
 with anybody else that I want.

742
00:30:10,360 --> 00:30:12,480
 I love that she's patient, so you know what?

743
00:30:12,480 --> 00:30:15,680
 I bet she won't mind if I don't help out around the house.

744
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,720
 That's insane.

745
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:21,360
 Like, I either respect all of who she is

746
00:30:21,360 --> 00:30:24,360
 or I disrespect all of who she is.

747
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:25,440
 And the same is true with God.

748
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:27,800
 You either have all of him or you have none of him.

749
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,960
 Some of him is not an option.

750
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:32,400
 That's how idolatry happens.

751
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,960
 So how does God react to idols?

752
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:38,600
 Well, this is what it says in verse seven.

753
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,200
 "And the Lord said to Moses,

754
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:46,040
 "Go down for your people whom you brought up

755
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:48,480
 "out of the land of Egypt have corrupted themselves."

756
00:30:48,480 --> 00:30:49,520
 What's interesting about that,

757
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:54,160
 it's the first time God has ever

758
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:59,160
 identified the people of Israel as not his own.

759
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:01,360
 It's the first time.

760
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:04,480
 He says in verse eight,

761
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:05,680
 "They have turned aside quickly out of the way

762
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:06,680
 "that I commanded them.

763
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:08,360
 "They have made for themselves a golden calf.

764
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:10,560
 "They've worshiped it and sacrificed to it.

765
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:13,760
 "And they said, these are your gods of Israel

766
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:15,120
 "who brought you up out of the land of Egypt."

767
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:15,960
 Isn't that interesting?

768
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:16,880
 God heard every word.

769
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:20,120
 "And the Lord said to Moses,

770
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:21,520
 "I've seen this people and behold,

771
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:23,200
 "it's a stiff-necked people.

772
00:31:23,200 --> 00:31:24,440
 "Now, therefore, let me alone

773
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:26,640
 "that my wrath may burn against them,

774
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:27,880
 "that I might consume them in order

775
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:30,160
 "that I might make a great nation of you."

776
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,520
 God's like, I'm done, man.

777
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:33,520
 I'll start over with you, Moses.

778
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:35,320
 And yet Moses, he goes on in the passage

779
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:36,840
 and he intercedes on behalf of the people

780
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:38,880
 and he asks God to reconsider.

781
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:41,680
 And what we see is that God ends up relenting.

782
00:31:41,680 --> 00:31:43,520
 But when we read this passage,

