 "Nevertheless, in the day when I visit,

1044
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:12,720
 "I will visit their sin upon them."

1045
00:43:12,720 --> 00:43:15,040
 It's interesting.

1046
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:18,480
 God makes a promise to deal with sin,

1047
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:25,200
 but he also honors a promise to let them live.

1048
00:43:25,200 --> 00:43:27,160
 How?

1049
00:43:27,160 --> 00:43:28,320
 How does that happen?

1050
00:43:28,320 --> 00:43:33,280
 Because God reacts to idolatry

1051
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:38,480
 different than how he responds to idolaters

1052
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:40,760
 that place their faith in him.

1053
00:43:40,760 --> 00:43:42,760
 Because although God's wrath

1054
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:46,240
 is terribly appropriate for idolatry,

1055
00:43:46,240 --> 00:43:51,240
 God's grace is wonderfully inappropriate for idolaters.

1056
00:43:51,240 --> 00:43:55,520
 Wonderfully inappropriate.

1057
00:43:55,520 --> 00:44:01,160
 And it's a grace that we see come

1058
00:44:01,160 --> 00:44:03,040
 through the man in the middle,

1059
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:04,960
 the one who stood in the gap,

1060
00:44:04,960 --> 00:44:07,440
 the one who stood between the people and God,

1061
00:44:07,440 --> 00:44:09,400
 because Moses asked God,

1062
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:12,320
 he said, "Blot out my life in the book of life."

1063
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:14,280
 He said, "Punish me rather than punish them."

1064
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:16,120
 He said, "I will stand in their place

1065
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,480
 "if only you'll let me."

1066
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:19,760
 He said, "I'll do anything for them,

1067
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:21,320
 "even at great cost to myself."

1068
00:44:21,320 --> 00:44:22,720
 And yet here's the thing.

1069
00:44:22,720 --> 00:44:25,080
 God looks at Moses and he says, "You can't.

1070
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:27,920
 "You can't do it.

1071
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:29,840
 "No man can.

1072
00:44:29,840 --> 00:44:34,840
 "You cannot be a sufficient sacrifice

1073
00:44:34,840 --> 00:44:36,080
 "for the sins of these people

1074
00:44:36,080 --> 00:44:39,320
 "because you need a sufficient sacrifice for your own sins."

1075
00:44:39,320 --> 00:44:42,760
 He says, "You cannot be the perfect life that they need

1076
00:44:42,760 --> 00:44:45,080
 "because you yourself do not have a perfect life."

1077
00:44:45,080 --> 00:44:47,440
 He says, "You can't bear the sins of the people

1078
00:44:47,440 --> 00:44:50,040
 "because you need someone to bear your sins.

1079
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:52,200
 "Instead, you can't do it, Moses.

1080
00:44:52,200 --> 00:44:54,360
 "No man can save my people

1081
00:44:54,360 --> 00:44:57,320
 "from the idolatry which they've indulged.

1082
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:59,920
 "But I can.

1083
00:44:59,920 --> 00:45:03,080
 "I can do it.

1084
00:45:05,280 --> 00:45:07,120
 "And I will do it."

1085
00:45:07,120 --> 00:45:09,920
 Because what we see in the cross

1086
00:45:09,920 --> 00:45:12,880
 are these two radical realities colliding.

1087
00:45:12,880 --> 00:45:15,840
 We see just how seriously God takes our sin

1088
00:45:15,840 --> 00:45:18,800
 and we see just how deeply God loves the sinner.

1089
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:21,480
 Because where Moses couldn't give his life,

1090
00:45:21,480 --> 00:45:23,160
 Jesus Christ has given his life.

1091
00:45:23,160 --> 00:45:24,880
 Where Moses could not make atonement,

1092
00:45:24,880 --> 00:45:28,080
 Christ has atoned for everyone who believes in him.

1093
00:45:28,080 --> 00:45:29,480
 Where Moses could not keep the law,

1094
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:31,520
 Jesus fulfilled the entire thing.

1095
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:34,040
 Where Moses went up the mountain to entreat the Lord,

1096
00:45:34,040 --> 00:45:37,200
 Jesus came down the mountain to entreat you

1097
00:45:37,200 --> 00:45:38,560
 and to entreat me.

1098
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:40,560
 What was his entreatment?

1099
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:43,160
 Believe and be saved.

1100
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:46,400
 In the weeks ahead,

1101
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:49,920
 we're gonna get very specific

1102
00:45:49,920 --> 00:45:54,920
 into money and pleasure and self and evil.

1103
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:58,680
 We will talk about all of it and what you do with it.

1104
00:45:58,680 --> 00:46:03,160
 And yet here tonight, the first thing we have to acknowledge

1105
00:46:04,680 --> 00:46:06,880
 is that we need someone to stand in the gap.

1106
00:46:06,880 --> 00:46:11,000
 That we cannot depose our idols on our own.

1107
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,120
 That's what's interesting.

1108
00:46:12,120 --> 00:46:14,120
 The people don't tear down their idol.

1109
00:46:14,120 --> 00:46:15,400
 Moses does it for them.

1110
00:46:15,400 --> 00:46:19,080
 You know what happens when you identify an idol

1111
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:19,920
 in your life?

1112
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:23,600
 You can't just turn away from it.

1113
00:46:23,600 --> 00:46:27,560
 What they do is they burn it up.

1114
00:46:27,560 --> 00:46:30,720
 They grind it to dust and they scatter it.

1115
00:46:30,720 --> 00:46:33,280
 They're done with it forever.

1116
00:46:33,280 --> 00:46:37,680
 Maybe tonight that's the step some of you need to take.

1117
00:46:37,680 --> 00:46:43,640
 Maybe tonight you need to actually get legitimately serious

1118
00:46:43,640 --> 00:46:46,320
 about the sin in your life.

1119
00:46:46,320 --> 00:46:48,320
 You need to ask someone to pray for you

1120
00:46:48,320 --> 00:46:51,560
 because the prayer of a righteous person has power

1121
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:54,840
 while it's working and you need some power in your life.

1122
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:58,880
 But no man stands in the gap, it's Christ who has.

1123
00:46:58,880 --> 00:47:02,240
 And so we plead the blood over every idol in our life, amen?

1124
00:47:02,240 --> 00:47:03,280
 Let me pray that you believe it.

1125
00:47:03,280 --> 00:47:04,120
 God, we love you.

1126
00:47:04,120 --> 00:47:06,520
 We need you.

1127
00:47:06,520 --> 00:47:10,560
 And we ask, oh God, as we take time here

1128
00:47:10,560 --> 00:47:12,040
 in this moment, right now,

1129
00:47:12,040 --> 00:47:17,760
 would you please move amongst the seats within our hearts

1130
00:47:17,760 --> 00:47:22,880
 and God, would you compel us to response?

1131
00:47:22,880 --> 00:47:27,080
 Lord, we don't, let me be very clear.

1132
00:47:27,080 --> 00:47:31,160
 God, we do not want to respond emotionally

1133
00:47:33,240 --> 00:47:36,200
 and check yourself on that.

1134
00:47:36,200 --> 00:47:39,000
 God, we don't want to respond emotionally

1135
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:42,880
 but what we do want is to respond convictionally.

1136
00:47:42,880 --> 00:47:45,560
 The spirit of God working in your heart,

1137
00:47:45,560 --> 00:47:49,200
 convicting you of something and take action on that.

1138
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:53,680
 God, we don't want to just create a space right now

1139
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:56,840
 where we performatively respond.

1140
00:47:56,840 --> 00:47:59,360
 God, we want to create a space right now

1141
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:02,360
 where we legitimately respond.

1142
00:48:02,360 --> 00:48:08,280
 And so we pray, oh God, would you help us

1143
00:48:08,280 --> 00:48:10,680
 to have the courage to do what we should,

1144
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:13,440
 to seek prayer down front if it's required,

1145
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:18,120
 to confess in the altar if it's what's needed,

1146
00:48:18,120 --> 00:48:22,880
 to lift our hands and worship the King that has saved.

1147
00:48:22,880 --> 00:48:26,040
 Help us, oh God, help us, oh God.

1148
00:48:26,040 --> 00:48:28,680
 We know not a single one of us can save ourselves

1149
00:48:28,680 --> 00:48:32,760
 but we need not do it for you, oh Christ, have done it.

1150
00:48:32,760 --> 00:48:35,200
 Maybe you're here and you've not placed your faith in Christ

1151
00:48:35,200 --> 00:48:37,120
 for the forgiveness of your sins.

1152
00:48:37,120 --> 00:48:39,040
 You can do it tonight.

1153
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:41,360
 You don't need to clean yourself up or earn anything more.

1154
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:43,880
 You just need to simply receive the gift of grace

1155
00:48:43,880 --> 00:48:48,720
 that is afforded through the loving kindness of Christ's

1156
00:48:48,720 --> 00:48:52,640
 perfect life, the sufficient death He died on your behalf,

1157
00:48:52,640 --> 00:48:54,880
 fulfilling the wages of your sin

1158
00:48:54,880 --> 00:48:59,440
 in the victorious resurrection where He conquered Satan,

1159
00:48:59,440 --> 00:49:03,840
 sin, and death for you that have faith in Him.

1160
00:49:03,840 --> 00:49:09,040
 And others of you, maybe you've gotten used to Him.

1161
00:49:09,040 --> 00:49:12,320
 Maybe you're discontent with Him.

1162
00:49:12,320 --> 00:49:17,000
 Maybe you've even redefined Him to fit your own desire.

1163
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:18,400
 Let's confess that stuff.

1164
00:49:18,400 --> 00:49:19,880
 Let's repent that stuff.

1165
00:49:19,880 --> 00:49:21,400
 Let's cast down our idols.

1166
00:49:21,400 --> 00:49:23,080
 Let's grind them to dust.

1167
00:49:23,080 --> 00:49:24,720
 Let's scatter them across the room

1168
00:49:24,720 --> 00:49:26,840
 and let's be finished with it here tonight.

1169
00:49:26,840 --> 00:49:29,040
 In the strong name of Christ we pray, amen.

